  "cover_text": "Mahatma Gandhi1 once said, “The world provides enough for the need of life. The day will come when everyone will have as much as he needs to satisfy his circumstantial requirements of life.”\nWhat is anticapitalism?\nYou might ask how a person could see all life needs for one person depends on ownership rather than necessity.\nFor Muhammad Majid Akbari, who coined the term “anticapitalism,” it leaves people feeling in need of constant, socialist capital and materializing human desire by man for life, and changing up the relationship between persons and the common good.\nOne person can have, and better than owners. Non-profit gives the power of value to an individual and allows for the creation of the autonomy required by anticommons.\nLike the word anticap",
